      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\mathbf{u} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we can use the cross product of these two vectors. The magnitude of the cross product of two vectors provides the area of the parallelogram formed by those vectors.\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is computed as follows:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{vmatrix} \n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4 \n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nExpanding along the first row, we have:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying each term:\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 + 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (14) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n\\]\n\\[\n= -2\\mathbf{i} - 14\\mathbf{j} - 10\\mathbf{k}\n\\]\n\nThe cross product \\(\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}\\) is:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector is given by the following equation:\n\\[\n|\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v}| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\nCalculating the magnitude:\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{300}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{100 \\times 3}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nContructing out the vectors :\n\\[\n\\mathbf{u} \\times \\mathbf{v} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nwe apply the magnitude to obtain the area of the parallelogram:\n\nHence:\n\\[\n\\boxed{20.0}\n\\]",
