      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the area of the parallelogram generated by two vectors, we use the fact that the area is given by the magnitude of the cross product of the two vectors.\n\nLet's denote the vectors as follows:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}, \\quad \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFirst, we compute the cross product \\(\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\):\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix}\n\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\\n3 & 1 & -2 \\\\\n1 & -3 & 4\n\\end{vmatrix}\n\\]\n\nExpanding this determinant:\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\mathbf{i} \\left(1 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot (-3)\\right) - \\mathbf{j} \\left(3 \\cdot 4 - (-2) \\cdot 1\\right) + \\mathbf{k} \\left(3 \\cdot (-3) - 1 \\cdot 1\\right)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (4 - 6) - \\mathbf{j} (12 - 2) + \\mathbf{k} (-9 - 1)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\mathbf{i} (-2) - \\mathbf{j} (10) + \\mathbf{k} (-10)\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -10 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nNext, we find the magnitude of this cross product vector:\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-10)^2 + (-10)^2}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{4 + 100 + 100}\n\\]\n\\[\n= \\sqrt{204}\n\\]\n\\[\n= 2\\sqrt{51}\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{2\\sqrt{51}}\n\\]",
